// ============================================================================
// Hevy Stats — part 00: header.
//
// Single-shortcut build. The .cherri source is split into lib/ parts (this
// file plus 10-input, 20-routine, 30-bodyweight, 40-analysis, 50-records,
// 60-output); build.py concatenates them in filename order and compiles the
// result. Cherri has no #include for code and Shortcuts has no subroutines,
// so each part is a "function" by convention: a clearly delimited section
// with a documented contract (inputs it reads, outputs it sets). The
// compiled shortcut is one linear action list; the part boundaries below
// are where you cut if you ever need a real callable unit.
//
// Function map:
//   parseInput()         in: ShortcutInput
//                        out: apiKey, bodyWeightTxt, outputFormat
//   fetchRoutine()       in: apiKey
//                        out: routineDict, routineName  (errFlag on failure)
//   resolveBodyWeight()  in: apiKey, bodyWeightTxt
//                        out: bodyWeightNum            (0 = unknown)
//   analyzeExercises()   in: apiKey, routineDict, bodyWeightNum, routineName
//                        out: resultJson               (stats as JSON text;
//                              errFlag on failure)
//   buildRecordMetrics() in: resultJson
//                        out: finalResult (stats Dictionary),
//                             records (List of RecordMetric Dictionaries),
//                             displayJson (records as JSON text, for show())
//   emitOutput()         in: errFlag, errMsg/errDetail/errStage,
//                            outputFormat, finalResult, records, displayJson,
//                            resultJson
//                        out: @out — the shortcut's result (ALWAYS the last
//                          action). One of:
//                          - List of RecordMetric Dictionaries
//                            (output_format "record_metrics", the default)
//                          - the stats Dictionary
//                            (output_format "stats")
//                          - {"_error", "_context"} on handled failure
//
// Input: Shortcut Input is either your Hevy API key as plain text, or a
//        JSON dictionary / Dictionary {
//          "api_key": "...", "body_weight_kg": 70, "output_format": "..."
//        }.
//        body_weight_kg is optional; when absent the latest Hevy body
//        measurement is used, else bodyweight sets get no weight metrics.
//        output_format is optional: "record_metrics" (default) or "stats".
//
// RecordMetric dictionaries have the shape of the "Record Metrics" form
// (see docs/RECORD_METRIC.md):
//   {"Form Name": "Hevy - Muscle Group" | "Hevy - Exercise" | "Hevy - Routine",
//    "Metric Name": "<subject> <metric>",
//    "Set Value": <number>, "Increment": false, "Decrement": false,
//    "Reset": false, "Increment Amount": ""}
// Records produced: per muscle group "<muscle> working sets" + "<muscle>
// volume"; per exercise "<exercise> volume" + "<exercise> 1RM"; routine
// "<routine> working sets" + "<routine> volume" + "<routine> duration"
// (duration skipped when unknown).
//
// Stats mirror src/hevy-stats.js (kept as the tested spec):
//   - working sets: routine sets whose type is normal/failure/dropset
//     (warmup excluded), grouped by the exercise's primary muscle group
//     ("other" when the template lookup misses).
//   - effective weight per history set: logged weight_kg when > 0, else the
//     body weight for bodyweight sets (weight_kg null/0) when known.
//   - 1RM: best Epley estimate (weight*(1+reps/30), true singles use the
//     weight itself) over qualifying history sets, rounded to 0.1 kg.
//     Exercises without a qualifying set are omitted.
//   - volume: sum of effective-weight x reps over the same qualifying sets
//     from the fetched history, per exercise and per muscle group,
//     rounded to 0.1 kg. Exercises with no volume are omitted.
//   - qualifying set: type normal/failure/dropset (warmup excluded),
//     effective weight > 0, reps 1..30.
//   - routineWorkingSets: total working sets prescribed in the routine
//     (every occurrence counts, same population as the per-muscle map).
//   - routineVolumeKg: sum of the rounded per-exercise volumes.
//   - routineDurationMinutes: minutes between start and end of the history
//     workout with the max workout_start_time whose workout_title matches
//     the routine title; null when none has both timestamps.
//   - body weight precedence: explicit body_weight_kg input > latest Hevy
//     body measurement with a weight > 0 > unknown.
//   - the first routine returned by the API is treated as most recently
//     updated.
//
// IMPORTANT: bare truthiness checks (`if @x` / `if !@x`) are NOT used
// anywhere here. Device testing (Sep 30, 2026) showed they misbehave.
// All emptiness checks use explicit `== @empty` / `!= @empty` comparisons
// and the error state uses a numeric flag.
//
// CHERRI GOTCHAS (each cost a device-test round trip):
//   - `@dict['key']` SILENTLY compiles to a plain variable copy, dropping
//     the key lookup. ALWAYS use getValue(@dict, "key").
//   - A double-quoted lone "{" or "}" (e.g. `@ob = "{"`) SILENTLY compiles
//     to empty text (the brace is read as an interpolation start).
//     Literal braces MUST be single-quoted: '{' / '}'. build.py fails the
//     build if a part contains the broken pattern.
//   - A custom `action` declaration MUST have a `: <type> {` body (even
//     empty); a bodyless declaration breaks `{@var}` parsing below it.
//
// NOTE: Get Contents of URL halts the shortcut with a system error on HTTP
// or network failures (e.g. a wrong API key -> 401); Shortcuts offers no
// try/catch for that. Everything else is handled below.

#define name Hevy Stats

#include 'actions/web'
#include 'actions/text'
#include 'actions/math'
#include 'actions/calendar'

// Raw Shortcuts action: Get Time Between Dates
// (is.workflow.actions.gettimebetweendates). Cherri 2.3.0 has no built-in
// for it; the schema below is verified against Apple's action definition
// (WFInput = second date, WFTimeUntilFromDate = first date, output =
// WFInput - WFTimeUntilFromDate) and against Daniel's own Stopwatch
// shortcut, which uses the same action. Unit is pinned to Minutes
// explicitly (the action default) rather than relied upon.
action 'is.workflow.actions.gettimebetweendates' timeBetweenDates(variable from: 'WFTimeUntilFromDate', variable to: 'WFInput'): number {
    "WFTimeUntilUnit": "Minutes"
}

// Get Value for Key with a VARIABLE key on a variable-typed dictionary.
// Same underlying action Cherri's getValue() emits
// (is.workflow.actions.getvalueforkey); declared raw because Cherri's
// type checker only accepts getValue() on dictionary-typed variables,
// while sub-dictionaries pulled out of another dictionary arrive untyped.
action 'is.workflow.actions.getvalueforkey' dictVal(variable dict: 'WFInput', text key: 'WFDictionaryKey'): variable {
    "WFGetDictionaryValueType": "Value"
}

// Get Keys from Dictionary on a variable-typed dictionary. Same underlying
// action Cherri's getKeys() emits (is.workflow.actions.getvalueforkey with
// "All Keys"); declared raw for the same type-checker reason as dictVal.
action 'is.workflow.actions.getvalueforkey' dictKeys(variable dict: 'WFInput'): array {
    "WFGetDictionaryValueType": "All Keys"
}

// Add to Variable (is.workflow.actions.appendvariable): appends the input
// to the named variable's list. The list is created up front with list().
action 'is.workflow.actions.appendvariable' listAdd(variable item: 'WFInput', text varName: 'WFVariableName'): variable {
}

// --- Shared state ----------------------------------------------------------
// Empty-text sentinel: Cherri only allows == / != between two variables.
@empty = ""
// Literal braces for hand-built JSON (single-quoted = raw, no interpolation).
@ob = '{'
@cb = '}'
// Working-set types, comma-padded so `contains` matches whole types only.
@okTypes = ",normal,failure,dropset,"
// Numeric error flag (0 = ok, 1 = error). Never tested with truthiness.
@errFlag = 0
@errMsg = ""
@errDetail = ""
@errStage = ""
